e":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-b2[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Add `@bead:` and `@agent:` artifact reference kinds[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]`@bead:sase-9z` and `@agent:9w` are first-class artifact references[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]everywhere the existing four builtin kinds already work — prompt [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]expansion, `sase artifact show/path/open`, the ACE `@` menu and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]prompt highlighting, the LSP, and ACE copy mode — resolving through[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]generated bead and agent pages with loud, actionable diagnostics [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]when a page has not been published yet.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]bead_and_agent_artifact_refs.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-b2[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-b2/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bead and agent reference grammar in sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]core_grammar[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core_grammar: add the `Bead { id }` and `Agent { name }` kind/payload [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wire variants with lexical-only validation, reject fragments on both, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bump the artifact-reference wire schema to 2, and make one shared [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]builtin-kind constant the single source of truth.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Local resolution and reverse canonicalization[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core_resolve[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core_grammar[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core_resolve: extend `ArtifactRefContextWire` with bead stores, agent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]roots, and the local agent owner; port bead page addressing into Rust; [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]implement `resolve_bead`/`resolve_agent` and the path-to-reference [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reverse mappings in `canonicalize_artifact_ref`.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Editor surfaces for the new kinds[/bold #D7AFFF]                             [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]core_editor[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core_resolve[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core_editor: teach the shared editor layer the two new kinds — [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]diagnostics now resolve them, the `@` kind menu lists them, and bounded [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]local payload enumeration lists bead ids and agent global names.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Python models and resolution context[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]py_facade[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core_resolve[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]py_facade: mirror the new kinds and wire schema in the Python [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]artifact-reference models and build the bead-store, agent-root, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent-owner context from local SASE storage without new hot-path I/O.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Prompt expansion and `sase artifact` support[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]py_cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after py_facade[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]py_cli: expand `@bead:`/`@agent:` to their page paths at launch, make [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`sase artifact show/path/open` accept the new kinds, and add [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]publication-aware hints to unresolved-reference errors.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ACE `@` menu payload rows for beads and agents[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]py_ace[dim] · [dim][/dim]after py_facade[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]py_ace: add bounded, off-thread bead and agent payload catalogs to the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]grouped `@` menu, with their own row badges, panel titles, and durable [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]insertions.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ACE copy mode yields bead and agent references[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]py_copy[dim] · [dim][/dim]after py_ace[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]py_copy: make `%@` on an epic/phase row copy `bead:<id>`, move the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]design plan reference to a new `%d` key, and add `%@` to the Agents tab.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation sweep[/bold #D7AFFF]                                           [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core_editor, py_cli, py_copy[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs: update the artifact-reference, ACE, editor, beads, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agents-sidecar documentation to describe the two new kinds, their page [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dependency, the no-fragment rule, and the single-project resolution [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]scope.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Raise the published `sase-core-rs` floor[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]pin[dim] · [dim][/dim]after docs[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pin: after the sase-core release publishes, raise the `sase-core-rs` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]floor to the version that first ships the wire-schema-2 [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]artifact-reference bindings, refresh the lock, and update the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]declared-minimum assertion.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-b2","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","phase_bead_id":"sase-b2.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-8d25789c9998070bab32282c0151b914","started_at":"2026-07-30T01:36:47.975322+00:00","state":"active"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1785382962,"sha":"40f61abb525eec988a3959c1449543502b7a0112","subject":"build(deps): raise the sase-core-rs floor to 0.12.17"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"72d4d0c6010eb2b93abfcff3f3a7561ab92d233d95d09e0e0793a51f95f9bf21","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-b2.9/chat.md","size_bytes":3281},"commits":{"digest":"8004cbe7d0c3e063b0b5e29bbb03acfd9b7b00c8058004c97ea2a2913341ce63","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-b2.9/commits.json","size_bytes":230},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-b2.9/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"d7feafef9ef3822b8b2c9148d5597062a654363ef35186a274fcc29383fa7118","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-b2.9/meta.json","size_bytes":599},"prompt":{"digest":"32bc5bb5becf715231dc87175c9b74a5e75d61bd0b3fb14653c78dadb909fbb7","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-b2.9/prompt.md","size_bytes":153},"state":{"digest":"854221c93ca6e4b3c10782167429bb572ca2a91e0d3f2956301db718868c7ca9","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-b2.9/state.json","size_bytes":180}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-b2.9","local_name":"sase-b2.9","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-b2","agent_clan_generation":"20260729213633","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-b2.9","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sas